# Project: Smart IoT Monitoring System — Backend
# Stack: Java 17, Spring Boot, MySQL 8, Docker
# Role: Backend Developer (Sprint 2)

## Package Structure
com.iot.backend
├── controller/
├── service/
├── repository/
├── entity/
├── dto/
├── mapper/
├── enums/
├── exception/
└── config/

## Naming Conventions
- Entities: PascalCase, no "Entity" suffix (e.g. TrafficSensorData)
- DTOs: [EntityName]RequestDTO / [EntityName]ResponseDTO
- Services: [EntityName]Service (interface) + [EntityName]ServiceImpl
- Repositories: [EntityName]Repository extends JpaRepository
- Controllers: [EntityName]Controller

## Non-Negotiables
- All primary keys: UUID (auto-generated)
- Passwords: BCrypt only, never plain
- Enums: stored as STRING in DB (@Enumerated(EnumType.STRING))
- Logging: SLF4J + Logback via @Slf4j (Lombok)
- Every log must include: timestamp, class, method, action, result/error
- Validation in THREE places: DTO annotations + Service layer + DB schema
- No business logic in controllers
- No DB calls in controllers
- Parameterized queries only (no string-concatenated SQL)

## Enums (all in com.iot.backend.enums)
- SensorType: TRAFFIC, AIR_POLLUTION, STREET_LIGHT
- CongestionLevel: LOW, MODERATE, HIGH, SEVERE
- PollutionLevel: GOOD, MODERATE, UNHEALTHY, HAZARDOUS
- LightStatus: ON, OFF, DIM
- Metric: VEHICLE_COUNT, CONGESTION_LEVEL, SPEED, PM2_5, PM10, NO2, SO2, POLLUTION_LEVEL, BRIGHTNESS, STATUS
- AlertType: ABOVE_THRESHOLD, BELOW_THRESHOLD

## HTTP Status Code Rules
- 200: successful GET
- 201: successful POST (resource created)
- 400: validation error / bad input
- 401: unauthenticated
- 403: unauthorized
- 404: resource not found
- 409: conflict (duplicate)
- 500: unexpected server error
- NEVER return 200 with an error body

## Scheduler Rules
- Cron: 0 */5 * * * * (every 5 minutes)
- Wrap every @Scheduled method in try/catch
- Log: start time, records inserted per type, end time, any exceptions
- ThreadPoolTaskScheduler must be explicitly configured

## API Rules
- Use nouns not verbs: /api/sensors not /api/getSensors
- Every endpoint: minimum 1 positive + 1 negative Postman test
- RESTful resource naming always plural

## What NOT to Do
- No @Transactional on controller methods
- No String ordinal for enums (always EnumType.STRING)
- No unhandled exceptions — every service method has try/catch or @ControllerAdvice handling
- No hardcoded credentials anywhere
- No skipping unit tests